      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DEVOTED TO YOU (6) is on a quick turnaround after a solid third over 2435m at Geelong seven days ago. Lot to like about the way he finished off there and there isn't anywhere near the depth in this contest. SEA DANGER (4) failed to figure again last time over 2435m at Geelong, beaten 8 lengths into seventh in the same race as DEVOTED TO YOU. Previous run was good, though, so might pay to give another chance. EYE TRACKER (8) was beaten just a neck last start and landed her first top-three finish in the process at Ballarat Synthetic over 2100m. Has taken a while to hit form and poses a serious threat again. SITAR (5) was beaten 9 lengths into fourth in a 2200m contest at Ballarat Synthetic at his latest appearance. Better than recent efforts suggest. ARES FLIGHT (1) has been building fitness all prep and might now be ready for this trip, which could spark an improved performance.",
